==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|cōdex}}

===Etymology===
Uncertain, but some have connected it to {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₃osk-||ash tree}}, the same source as Welsh {{m|cy|onnen}}, Latin {{m|la|ornus||wild mountain ash}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|úosis}}, Russian {{m|ru|я́сень}}, Albanian {{m|sq|ah||beech}}, Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ὀξύα||beech}}, Old Armenian {{m|xcl|հացի}}. The connection stems from the assumption that Indo-Europeans used hollowed out ash trees as boats and skiffs.<ref>{{R:ine:Schrader:1890}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|caudex}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|caudex||caudicis|m|third}}

# A [[tree trunk]], [[stump]].
# A [[bollard]]; [[post]].
# A [[book]], [[writing]]; [[notebook]], [[account book]].
# {{lb|la|pejorative}} A [[blockhead]], [[idiot]].

====Declension====
{{la-decl-3rd|caudex}}

